1
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:13,909
<i>Jonathan! Nancy! Jonathan!</i>

2
00:00:14,785 --> 00:00:16,370
Jonathan! Nancy!

3
00:00:17,747 --> 00:00:19,457
What the hell are you doing?

4
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:22,710
Listen to me! Don't touch anything!

5
00:00:36,557 --> 00:00:37,808
Maybe you missed?

6
00:00:54,784 --> 00:00:56,744
- Maybe we should, uh...
- Yeah.

7
00:01:40,746 --> 00:01:43,374
Before you say anything,
I know it's 5:00 in the morning,

8
00:01:43,457 --> 00:01:45,417
but I need you
to build me a telemetry tracker.

9
00:01:45,501 --> 00:01:47,294
What? Erica, it is--

10
00:01:47,378 --> 00:01:49,380
Five in the morning.
She led with that, buddy.

11
00:01:49,463 --> 00:01:51,632
I'm sorry. Who are you?

12
00:01:51,715 --> 00:01:53,759
- My uncle.
- Babysitter. Babysitter.

13
00:01:53,843 --> 00:01:55,136
Who is it, snookums?

14
00:01:55,219 --> 00:01:59,056
It's okay, sugar lump. Go back to bed.
I'll just be one second.

15
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:00,349
Okay.

16
00:02:00,432 --> 00:02:01,684
The librarian?

17
00:02:01,767 --> 00:02:03,853
You get too loud in the sack,
she shush you?

18
00:02:03,936 --> 00:02:10,192
Okay, listen. You and whoever you are,
this is highly inappropriate.

19
00:02:10,276 --> 00:02:12,361
I will see you in class, Erica.

20
00:02:13,487 --> 00:02:15,364
Dustin is in danger.

21
00:02:16,031 --> 00:02:18,159
Danger? What kind of danger?

22
00:02:18,242 --> 00:02:19,869
Like the life or death kind.

23
00:02:19,952 --> 00:02:23,038
What do you say, snookums?
You gonna keep playing with your bookworm,

24
00:02:23,122 --> 00:02:26,083
or you gonna build us our tracker
and save your star student?

25
00:02:29,253 --> 00:02:30,254
Henderson!

26
00:02:30,963 --> 00:02:32,298
Dustin!

27
00:02:32,381 --> 00:02:34,758
Dustin. Hey. What the hell was that?

28
00:02:34,842 --> 00:02:37,011
Was that the shield generator?
Did they find it?

29
00:02:37,094 --> 00:02:38,345
I was wrong.

30
00:02:38,846 --> 00:02:40,306
I was terribly,

31
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,058
catastrophically wrong.

32
00:02:43,142 --> 00:02:44,226
What?

33
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:46,353
After you left, I found a journal.

34
00:02:47,062 --> 00:02:48,647
<i>Brenner's journal.</i>

35
00:02:50,191 --> 00:02:53,402
<i>The key to destroying that wall
is in this lab,</i>

36
00:02:53,485 --> 00:02:56,071
<i>but it is not a shield generator.</i>

37
00:02:56,155 --> 00:02:58,657
It isn't dark magic. Vecna didn't make it.

38
00:03:02,077 --> 00:03:03,412
Science did.

39
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:08,000
<i>Theoretical physicists call it
exotic matter.</i>

40
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:12,087
A single source of energy
that is holding that giant wall together,

41
00:03:12,171 --> 00:03:14,590
and I think Nancy just shot it.

42
00:03:25,768 --> 00:03:28,562
<i>How is that bad? That's why
we're here, to get through this wall.</i>

43
00:03:28,646 --> 00:03:30,648
- You are not listening!
- I am listening.

44
00:03:30,731 --> 00:03:33,275
Vecna didn't make the wall.
So he isn't on the other side,

45
00:03:33,359 --> 00:03:36,320
which means Holly and the missing kids
aren't either. Nobody is.

46
00:03:37,613 --> 00:03:39,693
Then what the hell is
on the other side of that wall?

47
00:03:49,833 --> 00:03:51,126
Why'd it stop?

48
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:00,052
Dustin, what's on the other side
of the wall?

49
00:04:00,844 --> 00:04:01,844
Death.

50
00:04:04,974 --> 00:04:06,141
Whoa.

51
00:04:11,855 --> 00:04:14,525
Come on! Come on, let's go!

52
00:04:15,442 --> 00:04:16,819
Hurry! Hurry! Hurry!

53
00:04:17,528 --> 00:04:18,654
Let's go! Let's go!

54
00:04:19,363 --> 00:04:20,489
Get down! Get down!

55
00:04:30,708 --> 00:04:32,418
This whole time,

56
00:04:32,501 --> 00:04:35,671
<i>everything we have ever assumed
about the Upside Down has been</i>

57
00:04:36,505 --> 00:04:37,965
dead wrong.

58
00:04:43,012 --> 00:04:44,555
The gate!

59
00:04:44,638 --> 00:04:45,764
The gate!

60
00:04:46,890 --> 00:04:48,684
I can clear a path!

61
00:04:48,767 --> 00:04:52,855
No, no, no!
You stay behind... stay behind me!

62
00:04:52,938 --> 00:04:54,940
No! Goddamnit!

63
00:05:04,366 --> 00:05:05,367
No!

64
00:05:06,035 --> 00:05:07,077
No! No!

65
00:05:19,798 --> 00:05:22,426
This place, the Upside Down,

66
00:05:22,509 --> 00:05:26,013
<i>it isn't another dimension.
It's not another world.</i>

67
00:05:26,096 --> 00:05:27,723
<i>It's a wormhole.</i>

68
00:05:27,806 --> 00:05:28,807
A bridge

69
00:05:29,683 --> 00:05:33,812
between two points in time and space,
between our world and another.

70
00:05:33,896 --> 00:05:35,481
And if the bridge collapses?

71
00:05:35,564 --> 00:05:37,399
It will take us with it.

72
00:05:39,943 --> 00:05:41,070
All of us.

73
00:07:41,064 --> 00:07:42,524
Go, go, go, go!

74
00:07:47,488 --> 00:07:50,407
Are you okay? Are you okay? It's okay.

75
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,327
We're safe here.
He can't get us here, okay?

76
00:07:53,410 --> 00:07:54,411
Max...

77
00:08:03,879 --> 00:08:05,130
Holly!

78
00:08:05,881 --> 00:08:06,882
Come on.

79
00:08:10,844 --> 00:08:14,097
Holly, sweetheart.
Stop, or I'll hurt her.

80
00:08:16,225 --> 00:08:20,437
I know you believe Max is your friend.

81
00:08:21,063 --> 00:08:25,275
But she has tricked you, Holly.
She has corrupted your mind.

82
00:08:25,359 --> 00:08:27,236
She is a liar.

83
00:08:27,319 --> 00:08:29,655
No! No, you're the liar!

84
00:08:29,738 --> 00:08:32,032
I saw you! I saw what you really are!

85
00:08:32,115 --> 00:08:35,327
You're a monster! A disgusting monster!

86
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:36,870
Holly!

87
00:08:36,954 --> 00:08:40,541
If you don't come back with me right now
and rejoin the other children,

88
00:08:40,624 --> 00:08:43,293
I will have no choice but to hurt Max.

89
00:08:47,047 --> 00:08:49,174
I may even have to kill her.

90
00:08:49,258 --> 00:08:51,426
Then why don't you? Huh?

91
00:08:52,177 --> 00:08:53,095
I'm right here.

92
00:08:53,178 --> 00:08:54,930
Oh, that's right.

93
00:08:55,013 --> 00:08:59,309
You're too scared of a stupid cave,
you goddamn coward!

94
00:08:59,977 --> 00:09:02,813
Things have changed, Max.

95
00:09:03,855 --> 00:09:07,276
There are now other ways to get to you.

96
00:09:07,859 --> 00:09:08,944
And Holly?

97
00:09:09,987 --> 00:09:13,198
When your new friend begins to suffer,

98
00:09:14,616 --> 00:09:16,201
and she will suffer,

99
00:09:16,994 --> 00:09:20,205
you can either return to me
and end her suffering,

100
00:09:21,039 --> 00:09:23,417
or you can watch your new friend die.

101
00:09:24,251 --> 00:09:26,003
Her life is in your hands.

102
00:10:10,422 --> 00:10:14,968
<i>Can someone please explain to me
what the hell happened out there?</i>

103
00:10:15,052 --> 00:10:18,764
We burnt out the particles.
I watched them fly up the tower.

104
00:10:18,847 --> 00:10:21,266
- I mean, you guys saw that, right?
- Hard to miss.

105
00:10:21,350 --> 00:10:23,644
So Will should be unplugged
from the hive mind.

106
00:10:23,727 --> 00:10:25,812
- Theoretically.
- But why didn't he wake up?

107
00:10:25,896 --> 00:10:27,773
How did he see Max if she's with Holly?

108
00:10:27,856 --> 00:10:30,651
Is this real?
Is Vecna messing with us again?

109
00:10:30,734 --> 00:10:32,527
This makes no goddamn sense!

110
00:10:32,611 --> 00:10:37,115
The doctors, they never understood
why Max was in the coma, right?

111
00:10:37,199 --> 00:10:38,742
What? No. Why?

112
00:10:40,869 --> 00:10:43,955
Okay. Okay, okay, okay, okay.

113
00:10:44,039 --> 00:10:47,751
So let's just assume for a second
that everything that Will saw was real.

114
00:10:47,834 --> 00:10:50,087
- He saw Max. He saw Holly.
- Yeah, but how?

115
00:10:50,170 --> 00:10:53,215
I'm getting to that. Let's say that, uh...

116
00:10:54,091 --> 00:10:55,342
this is Will,

117
00:10:55,425 --> 00:10:58,845
and this is Holly.

118
00:10:58,929 --> 00:10:59,929
And...

119
00:11:00,389 --> 00:11:03,642
uh, this, of course, is Max.

120
00:11:04,601 --> 00:11:07,437
They're in three disparate locations,
the Squawk, the hospital,

121
00:11:07,521 --> 00:11:09,832
and some presently unknown place
in the Upside Down. Right?

122
00:11:09,856 --> 00:11:11,066
- Right.
- Yeah.

123
00:11:11,149 --> 00:11:14,820
But they share one very essential thing
in common.

124
00:11:14,903 --> 00:11:16,238
They're all unconscious.

125
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,220
What happens when Vecna captures you?

126
00:11:20,867 --> 00:11:22,077
You go into a trance.

127
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:24,246
Which would look
a heck of a lot like a coma.

128
00:11:24,329 --> 00:11:27,499
No wonder the doctors are so clueless.
Max was never in a coma.

129
00:11:27,582 --> 00:11:29,209
She was in a trance.

130
00:11:29,793 --> 00:11:32,713
Just like Will. Just like Holly.

131
00:11:33,296 --> 00:11:36,508
It is hitting me
like a Whitney Houston high note.

132
00:11:36,591 --> 00:11:38,176
What if their minds...

133
00:11:39,302 --> 00:11:40,721
are all in the same place?

134
00:11:41,805 --> 00:11:43,098
In Vecna's mind.

135
00:11:44,474 --> 00:11:45,559
Imprisoned.

136
00:11:46,601 --> 00:11:48,311
At least, they were.

137
00:11:48,395 --> 00:11:49,604
If Will's right,

138
00:11:49,688 --> 00:11:53,775
then Max and Holly
are now making a prison break.

139
00:11:53,859 --> 00:11:55,318
And if they succeed,

140
00:11:55,402 --> 00:11:58,780
they will return to their physical bodies,

141
00:11:59,573 --> 00:12:02,409
and Max will come back to life.

142
00:12:02,492 --> 00:12:05,287
And they'll have been
in Vecna's mind, literally.

143
00:12:05,370 --> 00:12:07,390
They'll know everything.
They'll know where Will is.

144
00:12:07,414 --> 00:12:09,684
- Where the kids are.
- They might even know what he's planning.

145
00:12:09,708 --> 00:12:12,753
- That's endgame.
- The fate of the planet may very well rest

146
00:12:12,836 --> 00:12:16,423
in the hands of your comatose girlfriend
and your baby sister.

147
00:12:16,506 --> 00:12:18,341
It's worth one more shot, right?

148
00:12:18,425 --> 00:12:19,968
- Can you drive?
- Not legally.

149
00:12:20,051 --> 00:12:22,171
Good enough.
Take Joyce's car. Do not get pulled over.

150
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:23,722
Get to Max. I'll stay with Will.

151
00:12:23,805 --> 00:12:24,806
Okay.

152
00:13:04,137 --> 00:13:06,181
Do you remember this place...

153
00:13:07,682 --> 00:13:08,683
William?

154
00:13:10,936 --> 00:13:13,146
No, no, no...

155
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:16,858
- Does it... bring back...
- No.

156
00:13:21,404 --> 00:13:22,614
memories?

157
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:25,659
Max, Holly...

158
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:28,829
They got away, didn't they?

159
00:13:30,247 --> 00:13:32,249
Did the leg slow you down?

160
00:13:32,332 --> 00:13:35,418
You think you are clever, don't you?

161
00:13:36,002 --> 00:13:41,341
But remember, I am the one.

162
00:13:41,925 --> 00:13:44,386
The one who invited you in.

163
00:13:45,512 --> 00:13:48,306
You were my vessel.

164
00:13:49,266 --> 00:13:50,767
My spy.

165
00:13:52,352 --> 00:13:54,104
My builder.

166
00:13:55,397 --> 00:13:56,398
Builder?

167
00:13:59,776 --> 00:14:03,238
How do you think the tunnels came to be,
William?

168
00:14:05,907 --> 00:14:08,910
You built them

169
00:14:08,994 --> 00:14:13,582
<i>each and every night you slept.</i>

170
00:14:20,005 --> 00:14:22,841
There is much power within you.

171
00:14:23,675 --> 00:14:26,386
But make no mistake, boy.

172
00:14:27,470 --> 00:14:30,348
They are my powers,

173
00:14:30,432 --> 00:14:34,644
and they are stronger than ever before.

174
00:14:38,982 --> 00:14:41,568
Much stronger.

175
00:14:51,995 --> 00:14:54,289
Now, at last, it is time.

176
00:14:55,415 --> 00:15:01,087
Time for my vessels
to lead us to a new world.

177
00:15:02,881 --> 00:15:04,424
A better world.

178
00:15:05,342 --> 00:15:10,013
Too bad your world will never exist,

179
00:15:10,096 --> 00:15:13,099
now that Max has one of your vessels.

180
00:15:13,683 --> 00:15:17,812
There are ways
to smoke a fox from its den, William.

181
00:15:17,896 --> 00:15:20,315
And you are going to help me.

182
00:15:20,398 --> 00:15:25,070
You are going to be my spy

183
00:15:25,153 --> 00:15:29,115
one last time.

184
00:15:29,199 --> 00:15:30,199
No.

185
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:31,700
Never.

186
00:15:42,295 --> 00:15:44,798
The more you resist...

187
00:15:46,216 --> 00:15:48,760
the more this will hurt.

188
00:16:15,787 --> 00:16:16,788
Stupid.

189
00:16:21,793 --> 00:16:23,128
- Hey!
- What are you doing?

190
00:16:23,211 --> 00:16:24,587
Seeing if he's still out there.

191
00:16:24,671 --> 00:16:25,880
- He's not.
- How do you know?

192
00:16:25,964 --> 00:16:28,717
Because he knows he can't get us in here.
Let's go.

193
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:32,053
He said that things had changed,
that there were other ways.

194
00:16:32,137 --> 00:16:35,181
Yeah, and he's totally full of shit.
You should know this by now.

195
00:16:35,265 --> 00:16:39,936
So we're supposed to what?
Just do nothing? Accept our fate?

196
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:41,396
No, we're not accepting shit.

197
00:16:41,479 --> 00:16:43,732
We're just staying alive
until we're rescued.

198
00:16:43,815 --> 00:16:45,817
- Rescued by Eleven?
- Mm-hmm.

199
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,277
How do you know that was even her?

200
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:49,654
Unless you know somebody else
with psychic powers

201
00:16:49,738 --> 00:16:52,198
who's able
to remotely infiltrate Vecna's mind,

202
00:16:52,282 --> 00:16:56,327
fight him off, communicate through him
to tell us to run, then it had to be El.

203
00:16:56,411 --> 00:16:59,497
Which means she knows we're here,
and she'll come and she'll save us.

204
00:16:59,581 --> 00:17:01,666
Now, can you please stop pacing?

205
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:04,294
Seriously, you're starting
to remind me of your brother.

206
00:17:08,256 --> 00:17:09,299
Thank you.

207
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:17,974
Why can't Henry
come in here anyway?

208
00:17:18,058 --> 00:17:19,267
I don't know.

209
00:17:20,435 --> 00:17:22,771
You've had two years with nothing to do.

210
00:17:24,022 --> 00:17:25,482
You must have a theory.

211
00:17:28,818 --> 00:17:31,988
If we're just waiting,
we might as well talk.

212
00:17:38,787 --> 00:17:40,163
- This prison...
- Camazotz.

213
00:17:40,246 --> 00:17:42,290
Camazotz. Sure.

214
00:17:44,542 --> 00:17:47,253
It's made up of Henry's memories, right?

215
00:17:47,837 --> 00:17:50,465
Including this cave.

216
00:17:50,548 --> 00:17:54,219
So I figure it's like,

217
00:17:54,719 --> 00:17:56,930
I don't know,
a memory that, for whatever reason,

218
00:17:57,013 --> 00:17:59,349
Henry doesn't want to face.

219
00:18:00,391 --> 00:18:01,768
Something traumatic.

220
00:18:03,436 --> 00:18:07,732
Except there's nothing in here
that is even remotely scary, so...

221
00:18:08,441 --> 00:18:09,651
maybe not.

222
00:18:11,945 --> 00:18:13,530
Anyway, that's my theory.

223
00:18:15,031 --> 00:18:16,032
I like it.

224
00:18:18,493 --> 00:18:19,493
Thanks.

225
00:18:19,994 --> 00:18:22,872
And if you're right,

226
00:18:24,457 --> 00:18:27,460
maybe we can escape through this memory.

227
00:18:28,044 --> 00:18:29,379
- What?
- Okay, so...

228
00:18:30,255 --> 00:18:33,508
My house, your attic,
those were traumatic memories too,

229
00:18:33,591 --> 00:18:35,468
and they led us out of Camazotz.

230
00:18:35,552 --> 00:18:38,096
So maybe Henry's memory can too.

231
00:18:38,179 --> 00:18:41,057
First of all, there's nothing in here,
as I said.

232
00:18:41,141 --> 00:18:43,977
Secondly, our memories
weren't simply traumatic.

233
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:47,564
They were memories of the precise moment
that Henry stole our minds.

234
00:18:47,647 --> 00:18:49,732
And he can't steal his own mind, can he?

235
00:18:49,816 --> 00:18:53,236
- How do you know?
- Because that makes no sense.

236
00:18:53,319 --> 00:18:55,572
And everything in this place makes sense?

237
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:58,741
I mean,

238
00:18:59,742 --> 00:19:01,369
maybe there's like a...

239
00:19:02,203 --> 00:19:04,998
a secret passageway or something.

240
00:19:05,081 --> 00:19:08,376
Right, yes, I totally forgot
about the secret passage.

241
00:19:12,255 --> 00:19:13,256
What about out there?

242
00:19:13,339 --> 00:19:15,633
Sand. Lots of sand.

243
00:19:16,301 --> 00:19:17,510
- You've searched it?
- Yes.

244
00:19:17,594 --> 00:19:19,387
- All of it?
- It goes on for miles.

245
00:19:19,971 --> 00:19:20,972
So, no.

246
00:19:23,892 --> 00:19:25,476
You are not going out there.

247
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:29,355
Holly, we're staying here,
and we wait for Eleven, end of story.

248
00:19:29,439 --> 00:19:30,773
I don't think Henry was bluffing

249
00:19:30,857 --> 00:19:32,942
when he said
there's another way to get to you.

250
00:19:33,026 --> 00:19:36,154
We have to find a way out of here
before that happens.

251
00:19:36,946 --> 00:19:37,946
You coming?

252
00:19:38,448 --> 00:19:41,201
Or are you gonna let
a child head into the desert unsupervised?

253
00:19:42,702 --> 00:19:43,786
I take it back.

254
00:19:43,870 --> 00:19:47,332
You don't remind me of your brother.
You <i>are</i> your brother!

255
00:20:01,262 --> 00:20:02,263
Joyce?

256
00:20:03,681 --> 00:20:05,041
Did someone call the funeral home?

257
00:20:16,486 --> 00:20:17,737
Mike.

258
00:20:21,241 --> 00:20:22,283
El!

259
00:20:22,367 --> 00:20:23,576
Oh, Mike...

260
00:20:30,875 --> 00:20:32,085
I'm here now.

261
00:20:33,002 --> 00:20:34,337
You're okay.

262
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:35,588
I'm okay.

263
00:20:36,673 --> 00:20:38,091
This is Kali,

264
00:20:38,675 --> 00:20:39,884
my sister.

265
00:20:39,968 --> 00:20:41,636
And this must be the famous Mike.

266
00:20:42,762 --> 00:20:44,681
I don't... I don't understand.

267
00:20:44,764 --> 00:20:48,184
It's a long story.
Probably best just to tell it once.

268
00:20:49,185 --> 00:20:51,145
Where's the rest of our greeting party?

269
00:20:55,692 --> 00:20:57,110
He's just in here.

270
00:21:04,492 --> 00:21:05,827
Oh, Jesus.

271
00:21:06,703 --> 00:21:08,121
How long has he been like this?

272
00:21:08,204 --> 00:21:09,289
A few hours.

273
00:21:10,581 --> 00:21:13,042
Do you think you can find him?

274
00:21:19,048 --> 00:21:21,634
Any clue in there about how long
it takes a wormhole to collapse?

275
00:21:21,718 --> 00:21:22,719
Ten minutes, maybe 20?

276
00:21:22,802 --> 00:21:24,887
I thought it'd be instantaneous.
Clearly not.

277
00:21:24,971 --> 00:21:27,157
- Why do you sound disappointed?
- I'm not disappointed.

278
00:21:27,181 --> 00:21:28,933
- You sound disappointed.
- I'm confused.

279
00:21:29,017 --> 00:21:31,311
As far as I see it,
there are two possibilities.

280
00:21:31,394 --> 00:21:34,022
Either this is the afterlife,
and you and I are spirits.

281
00:21:34,105 --> 00:21:35,207
- Which seems unlikely.
- Ooh.

282
00:21:35,231 --> 00:21:39,444
Or Nancy didn't completely destroy
the exotic matter.

283
00:21:39,527 --> 00:21:42,822
Because if she did, the walls
of the wormhole would have collapsed.

284
00:21:42,905 --> 00:21:44,949
And we would have been sucked
into oblivion.

285
00:21:45,033 --> 00:21:47,076
Okay, so what
are we waiting around here for?

286
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,202
Where are you going?

287
00:21:48,286 --> 00:21:50,955
To see if I can get a damn signal
to find Nancy.

288
00:21:51,039 --> 00:21:52,790
- Steve, wait.
- Let's go, Henderson.

289
00:21:52,874 --> 00:21:54,167
- Wait!
- Let's go.

290
00:21:55,001 --> 00:21:57,503
Steve, we don't know if it's safe up here.

291
00:21:57,587 --> 00:21:59,380
You said
the exotic matter wasn't destroyed.

292
00:21:59,464 --> 00:22:01,424
No, I said
it was not completely destroyed.

293
00:22:01,507 --> 00:22:03,676
But it was very clearly disturbed.

294
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:07,930
We have no idea what effect this will have
on matter, space-time, gravity.

295
00:22:08,014 --> 00:22:09,766
This whole building could very well be

296
00:22:09,849 --> 00:22:12,477
a highly unstable,
physics-defying death trap.

297
00:22:12,560 --> 00:22:14,187
It seems pretty stable to me.

298
00:22:14,270 --> 00:22:16,981
Nancy, you copy? Jonathan, are you there?

299
00:22:17,982 --> 00:22:18,982
Hello?

300
00:22:22,570 --> 00:22:24,447
Mother of God.

301
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:34,791
Please tell me they're not up there.

302
00:22:59,065 --> 00:23:01,901
No, no, no, no. No! Nancy!

303
00:23:05,196 --> 00:23:07,615
Nancy! No, no, no.

304
00:23:07,698 --> 00:23:08,698
Nancy!

305
00:23:08,741 --> 00:23:10,827
Come on. Nancy.

306
00:23:10,910 --> 00:23:12,829
Come on. Come on.

307
00:23:12,912 --> 00:23:15,623
- Are you okay? Are you okay? Okay.
- Yeah. I think so.

308
00:23:16,499 --> 00:23:17,500
What happened?

309
00:23:18,376 --> 00:23:19,919
I don't know. I don't know.

310
00:23:21,712 --> 00:23:23,089
I guess we fell.

311
00:23:23,172 --> 00:23:25,216
And also clearly didn't destroy it.

312
00:23:25,299 --> 00:23:26,801
Just pissed it off.

313
00:23:29,053 --> 00:23:30,471
Come on. Let's go.

314
00:23:33,099 --> 00:23:34,892
Let's get the hell out of here.

315
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:39,605
- Where's the door?
- Shit, shit.

316
00:23:40,273 --> 00:23:42,358
It's there. Come on.

317
00:23:46,362 --> 00:23:47,362
Shit!

318
00:23:50,199 --> 00:23:53,744
No, no, no! Shit! Shit! No, no, no, no!

319
00:23:56,664 --> 00:23:58,166
Goddamnit.

320
00:23:59,584 --> 00:24:00,877
Come on!

321
00:24:22,023 --> 00:24:25,526
Nancy, she didn't leave
a note or anything at the church?

322
00:24:25,610 --> 00:24:28,196
No. No, nothing.

323
00:24:28,696 --> 00:24:31,657
Which means they're either
a bunch of inconsiderate pricks,

324
00:24:32,241 --> 00:24:34,118
or they got captured by the military.

325
00:24:34,202 --> 00:24:37,830
To put your mind at ease, I am heavily
leaning on the inconsiderate prick theory.

326
00:24:37,914 --> 00:24:41,501
Wait, and that flesh wall you found,
you don't think...

327
00:24:41,584 --> 00:24:44,295
They got sucked into
the giant vacuum cleaner? No, I don't.

328
00:24:45,379 --> 00:24:48,549
But I don't really know, Mike.
I'm as confused as you.

329
00:24:49,258 --> 00:24:54,472
This whole thing, Max, Holly, this wall,
it's all gotta connect somehow,

330
00:24:54,555 --> 00:24:55,635
but I can't figure out how.

331
00:24:55,681 --> 00:24:58,809
It's like
there's a missing piece of the puzzle.

332
00:24:58,893 --> 00:24:59,769
A big piece.

333
00:24:59,852 --> 00:25:03,481
The pieces are in Vecna's mind,
and now we finally have a way to get in.

334
00:25:03,564 --> 00:25:05,650
Except Jane hasn't found anything.

335
00:25:06,484 --> 00:25:09,529
Oh, boy! Here comes Pollyanna
to brighten everybody's day.

336
00:25:09,612 --> 00:25:11,113
She's struggling up there.

337
00:25:11,197 --> 00:25:13,324
Oh, yeah?
Maybe you should give her some time.

338
00:25:13,407 --> 00:25:15,493
She's getting weaker, not stronger.

339
00:25:15,576 --> 00:25:19,038
So you are the expert on El, huh?

340
00:25:19,121 --> 00:25:20,998
You've known her for what,
a day and a half?

341
00:25:21,082 --> 00:25:23,209
Longer than you, actually.

342
00:25:23,292 --> 00:25:27,004
We were raised together,
and her name is Jane.

343
00:25:27,088 --> 00:25:29,048
- Jane Hopper.
- I'm just here to help.

344
00:25:29,131 --> 00:25:32,343
You're just here to help.
Well, I'm sorry I'm all out of gratitude.

345
00:25:32,426 --> 00:25:34,146
I thought you said
this fight was pointless.

346
00:25:34,220 --> 00:25:35,972
You said this whole thing was pointless?

347
00:25:36,055 --> 00:25:37,348
I never said that.

348
00:25:37,431 --> 00:25:40,393
Really? It sure as shit sounded to me
like you did.

349
00:25:40,476 --> 00:25:43,330
I leave you alone for two seconds with El,
and you worm your way into her head.

350
00:25:43,354 --> 00:25:46,524
She's probably having trouble finding Will
because you've thrown her off track.

351
00:25:46,607 --> 00:25:49,485
She was off track when I met her
because of you.

352
00:25:49,569 --> 00:25:50,903
Because of your lies.

353
00:25:50,987 --> 00:25:52,405
Everything I have done...

354
00:25:52,488 --> 00:25:55,533
...is to protect her.
Keep telling yourself that,

355
00:25:55,616 --> 00:25:58,828
but if you really want to protect her,
she needs to know the truth,

356
00:25:58,911 --> 00:26:01,872
and she needs to be ready
to deal with what's waiting for her

357
00:26:01,956 --> 00:26:03,666
on the other side of this.

358
00:26:04,166 --> 00:26:07,378
Killing Henry won't end this.

359
00:26:07,461 --> 00:26:08,461
What does that mean?

360
00:26:08,504 --> 00:26:13,259
It means nothing. She's a child.
She has no idea what she's talking about.

361
00:26:13,342 --> 00:26:15,136
She's talking a bunch of nonsense.

362
00:26:15,219 --> 00:26:17,179
I think you know I'm not.

363
00:26:18,389 --> 00:26:22,727
But just as you lie to Jane,
you also lie to yourself.

364
00:26:25,146 --> 00:26:27,773
You ask why I'm still here?

365
00:26:29,525 --> 00:26:34,488
I'm here to make sure
that this never happens again.

366
00:26:41,078 --> 00:26:42,078
El.

367
00:26:46,334 --> 00:26:47,335
El!

368
00:26:48,044 --> 00:26:49,712
Hey, is everything okay?

369
00:26:51,005 --> 00:26:53,716
I can't reach him. He keeps slipping away.

370
00:26:53,799 --> 00:26:55,801
Well, we have plenty of food in there,

371
00:26:55,885 --> 00:26:58,971
so eat, rest, and recharge your battery,
and we'll try it again.

372
00:26:59,055 --> 00:27:00,056
Or...

373
00:27:00,973 --> 00:27:02,433
we improve your signal.

374
00:27:03,017 --> 00:27:04,870
- The tank.
- Yeah. It'll take a while to set up.

375
00:27:04,894 --> 00:27:06,771
But you've gotta
recharge your battery anyway.

376
00:27:06,854 --> 00:27:10,566
Plus, that thing was a pain to build,
so I'd like to get some use out of it.

377
00:27:18,407 --> 00:27:21,202
- Doris, I'm gonna sign in later.
- I'm here for emotional support.

378
00:27:21,285 --> 00:27:23,287
Miss Buckley! Miss Buckley!

379
00:27:23,371 --> 00:27:25,581
Oh! You know what?

380
00:27:28,125 --> 00:27:29,251
Hey.

381
00:27:29,335 --> 00:27:30,961
- We need to talk.
- Yeah.

382
00:27:31,045 --> 00:27:33,089
- Wait, Robin!
- I've gotta deal with this. Just go!

383
00:27:33,172 --> 00:27:34,173
What about the plan?

384
00:27:34,256 --> 00:27:35,424
Vickie.

385
00:27:37,051 --> 00:27:39,804
Listen, I know you're pissed,
and you have every right to be.

386
00:27:39,887 --> 00:27:41,740
- They're looking for you.
- Who is looking for me?

387
00:27:41,764 --> 00:27:43,683
- Security. MPs.
- Why?

388
00:27:43,766 --> 00:27:46,203
- You wanna play dumb?
- I have no idea what you're talking about.

389
00:27:46,227 --> 00:27:47,853
Okay, all right, let me give you a hint.

390
00:27:47,937 --> 00:27:50,398
You, Mr. Bailey's room, benzos.

391
00:27:51,107 --> 00:27:52,525
Well, does it ring a bell yet?

392
00:27:52,608 --> 00:27:57,488
Robin, you've gotta start telling me
what is going on with you right now.

393
00:28:03,035 --> 00:28:05,996
Okay, Max, time to come home.

394
00:28:21,345 --> 00:28:23,305
I think
we've been at this long enough.

395
00:28:23,389 --> 00:28:25,433
We've searched
an inch of this place.

396
00:28:25,516 --> 00:28:27,435
At last, you get my point.

397
00:28:27,518 --> 00:28:30,563
I've spent I don't know how long
searching out here, but too long.

398
00:28:30,646 --> 00:28:33,649
You're not gonna just suddenly find
something that I haven't, okay?

399
00:28:33,733 --> 00:28:36,569
Did my brother ever tell you
about Uncle Eric?

400
00:28:36,652 --> 00:28:37,820
Uncle Eric?

401
00:28:37,903 --> 00:28:40,406
He's a metal detectorist.
Do you know what that is?

402
00:28:40,489 --> 00:28:41,782
He searches for metal.

403
00:28:41,866 --> 00:28:43,617
Yeah, with his metal detector.

404
00:28:43,701 --> 00:28:47,288
Looking for super old treasures and stuff
that dead people have left in the ground.

405
00:28:47,371 --> 00:28:50,499
Anyway, his favorite place to search is
Indiana Beach Amusement Park.

406
00:28:50,583 --> 00:28:52,668
I mean, he searched there for years,

407
00:28:52,752 --> 00:28:55,087
but all he ever found
was a bunch of cheap trinkets.

408
00:28:55,171 --> 00:28:58,674
Then one day, he opens up the newspaper
and boom, front page,

409
00:28:58,758 --> 00:29:00,885
some random tourist found a tin can

410
00:29:00,968 --> 00:29:04,054
filled with gold and silver coins
worth like millions of dollars.

411
00:29:04,138 --> 00:29:07,349
Right, so let me guess,
in this scenario, I'm Uncle Eric...

412
00:29:07,433 --> 00:29:08,726
And I'm the tourist.

413
00:29:19,111 --> 00:29:20,321
So stupid.

414
00:29:37,546 --> 00:29:38,964
"M" marks the spot.

415
00:29:43,719 --> 00:29:45,304
- Where are you going?
- I have an idea.

416
00:29:45,387 --> 00:29:47,306
- What idea?
- I'll show you when we're closer.

417
00:29:47,389 --> 00:29:49,892
- Holly!
- You said you wanted to go back.

418
00:29:49,975 --> 00:29:51,602
Well, we're going back.

419
00:29:54,021 --> 00:29:57,316
Guys, if you can hear us, we're coming.
I repeat, we're coming.

420
00:29:57,399 --> 00:30:00,319
Steve, slow down! The higher we go,
the more dangerous it gets.

421
00:30:00,402 --> 00:30:02,071
All the more reason to speed up.

422
00:30:02,154 --> 00:30:04,281
We're no use to them if we're dead. Steve!

423
00:30:13,457 --> 00:30:14,750
As I was saying...

424
00:30:20,339 --> 00:30:21,340
Come on!

425
00:30:21,423 --> 00:30:22,883
Damn it!

426
00:30:30,266 --> 00:30:31,684
What are you doing?

427
00:30:31,767 --> 00:30:35,020
A few floors down, it looked like one
of those soldiers cut through that door.

428
00:30:41,986 --> 00:30:43,279
Watch out.

429
00:30:47,867 --> 00:30:49,243
Shit! Get back!

430
00:30:52,329 --> 00:30:53,998
Shit! Shit!

431
00:30:54,081 --> 00:30:55,249
Oh, God!

432
00:31:01,964 --> 00:31:02,965
Holy shit!

433
00:31:05,593 --> 00:31:08,095
The table! Get to the table!

434
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:19,565
Now what?

435
00:31:26,030 --> 00:31:28,073
Help! Help!

436
00:31:28,157 --> 00:31:30,451
- Help! Help!
- Steve!

437
00:31:30,534 --> 00:31:33,662
- Help! Help!
- Hey! Help!

438
00:31:33,746 --> 00:31:36,874
- Help! Help! Help!
- Help! Help! Help!

439
00:32:12,034 --> 00:32:13,077
Almost ready out here.

440
00:32:17,164 --> 00:32:18,499
El's gonna fix this.

441
00:32:19,625 --> 00:32:20,834
She's gonna fix it.

442
00:32:25,172 --> 00:32:27,257
It was my idea, Hop.

443
00:32:28,592 --> 00:32:29,592
It was...

444
00:32:30,052 --> 00:32:32,596
my idea for him to go in there.

445
00:32:33,180 --> 00:32:35,641
I don't know. I just thought maybe,

446
00:32:35,724 --> 00:32:40,145
after everything that happened,
after everything I saw him do, that...

447
00:32:40,938 --> 00:32:43,273
I started thinking maybe all this time

448
00:32:43,357 --> 00:32:46,694
that I've been trying so hard
to protect him,

449
00:32:46,777 --> 00:32:49,279
I've really just been holding him back

450
00:32:51,031 --> 00:32:52,741
by not listening to him,

451
00:32:53,492 --> 00:32:55,202
not trusting him.

452
00:32:55,285 --> 00:32:56,704
And so if I just...

453
00:32:57,830 --> 00:33:01,458
I don't know.
If I just believed and let go,

454
00:33:01,542 --> 00:33:04,920
that, I don't know,
somehow this could all work out. And...

455
00:33:06,255 --> 00:33:11,385
It's like every choice
that I make is wrong.

456
00:33:11,468 --> 00:33:12,511
I know.

457
00:33:14,013 --> 00:33:18,183
I mean, you can push them into situations
they might not be ready for.

458
00:33:18,267 --> 00:33:20,853
You can be like me,
and you can be overprotective,

459
00:33:20,936 --> 00:33:23,272
and they just resent you for that.

460
00:33:23,355 --> 00:33:25,858
Joyce, one of the joys of being a parent...

461
00:33:28,402 --> 00:33:30,863
is that you'll have a constant reminder
your whole life

462
00:33:30,946 --> 00:33:32,740
that every choice you've made

463
00:33:33,532 --> 00:33:34,992
has been wrong.

464
00:33:38,537 --> 00:33:40,080
It's not on you, Joyce.

465
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:44,209
It's not on you.

466
00:33:59,892 --> 00:34:02,186
That looks nice.
Murray find that for you?

467
00:34:02,895 --> 00:34:03,896
Yeah.

468
00:34:05,773 --> 00:34:07,483
Santa Claus has good taste.

469
00:34:11,987 --> 00:34:14,406
Hey. Back at the Squawk,

470
00:34:15,157 --> 00:34:17,618
Kali, she said something weird

471
00:34:17,701 --> 00:34:20,871
about this not being over
even if we kill Henry.

472
00:34:20,954 --> 00:34:22,706
Do you know what she's talking about?

473
00:34:23,749 --> 00:34:25,167
It doesn't matter.

474
00:34:25,876 --> 00:34:27,211
I should warm this up.

475
00:34:27,836 --> 00:34:31,048
Okay, well, if it doesn't matter,
then why was Hop so angry at her?

476
00:34:31,131 --> 00:34:32,424
It's nothing, Mike, really.

477
00:34:32,508 --> 00:34:34,259
- Friends don't lie.
- I'm not lying.

478
00:34:34,343 --> 00:34:37,679
You're avoiding. That's a cheat.
I just want to help.

479
00:34:37,763 --> 00:34:40,224
You can't help. Not with this.

480
00:34:40,307 --> 00:34:42,101
Let me be the judge of that.

481
00:34:44,269 --> 00:34:45,437
El, come on.

482
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:52,945
There's a lab in the Upside Down.

483
00:34:53,028 --> 00:34:55,572
They're restarting Papa's program.

484
00:34:56,532 --> 00:34:58,283
Trying to make new numbers.

485
00:35:01,995 --> 00:35:03,080
The military?

486
00:35:06,458 --> 00:35:07,751
Okay.

487
00:35:07,835 --> 00:35:11,964
So, after we kill Vecna,
we destroy this new lab.

488
00:35:12,047 --> 00:35:13,757
End the program. Like a side quest.

489
00:35:13,841 --> 00:35:16,260
Mike, no, you don't understand.

490
00:35:16,343 --> 00:35:19,471
They don't need a lab to make new numbers.

491
00:35:19,555 --> 00:35:20,848
Henry's blood.

492
00:35:22,516 --> 00:35:23,725
It's in me.

493
00:35:23,809 --> 00:35:25,519
I'm not a monster.

494
00:35:26,770 --> 00:35:28,230
I know that now.

495
00:35:28,814 --> 00:35:30,858
But with me, with my blood,

496
00:35:32,025 --> 00:35:34,403
they can make more monsters.

497
00:35:35,529 --> 00:35:37,739
They can make more Henrys.

498
00:35:38,323 --> 00:35:40,284
The military will always be looking
for you.

499
00:35:40,367 --> 00:35:43,412
We've always known that.
Which is why we aren't staying in Hawkins.

500
00:35:43,495 --> 00:35:46,373
When this is all over, we're leaving.

501
00:35:46,456 --> 00:35:49,334
Escaping to some far off land. Remember?

502
00:35:49,418 --> 00:35:51,587
Somewhere where they can't find us.

503
00:35:52,337 --> 00:35:55,465
Somewhere
where there's at least one waterfall.

504
00:35:56,466 --> 00:35:57,467
Mike.

505
00:35:59,261 --> 00:36:02,514
This isn't like one of your campaigns.

506
00:36:03,640 --> 00:36:05,392
You don't get to write the ending.

507
00:36:06,185 --> 00:36:07,352
Not this time.

508
00:36:09,146 --> 00:36:10,355
Maybe I don't.

509
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:12,691
But <i>we</i> do.

510
00:36:12,774 --> 00:36:16,236
You, me, Lucas, Will, and Dustin.

511
00:36:16,820 --> 00:36:18,363
Because this is our story.

512
00:36:19,489 --> 00:36:21,825
And it starts with getting Will back.

513
00:36:38,175 --> 00:36:39,175
Max.

514
00:36:49,186 --> 00:36:52,439
You realize you don't need
your spyglass anymore? That's my cave.

515
00:36:52,522 --> 00:36:53,357
Yep.

516
00:36:53,440 --> 00:36:54,983
Also, the cap is still on.

517
00:36:55,484 --> 00:36:56,485
Yep.

518
00:36:57,402 --> 00:36:58,403
Look.

519
00:36:59,738 --> 00:37:00,822
Cap on.

520
00:37:06,119 --> 00:37:08,080
Okay, it's very dark.

521
00:37:08,163 --> 00:37:09,081
But not totally.

522
00:37:09,164 --> 00:37:10,666
You see that cutout of light?

523
00:37:10,749 --> 00:37:12,918
It's in the same shape
as the cave entrance.

524
00:37:13,001 --> 00:37:15,545
What are the chances
it cracks in the same shape as the cave,

525
00:37:15,629 --> 00:37:17,339
the cave we know Henry visited?

526
00:37:17,422 --> 00:37:20,717
I think the cap is a map,
a map Henry made when he was young,

527
00:37:20,801 --> 00:37:23,220
a map that'll lead us
to some kind of secret location.

528
00:37:24,054 --> 00:37:26,306
We just have to get the shapes to line up.

529
00:37:27,557 --> 00:37:30,060
And you think in this secret location,
we'll find what?

530
00:37:30,143 --> 00:37:31,603
Henry's traumatic memory?

531
00:37:31,687 --> 00:37:34,189
That. And a way out of Camazotz.

532
00:37:35,065 --> 00:37:37,317
At least... that's my theory.

533
00:37:38,277 --> 00:37:39,736
- I like it.
- Thanks.

534
00:37:39,820 --> 00:37:42,030
There's one tiny hole
in your theory, though.

535
00:37:42,114 --> 00:37:44,825
We're near the secret location,
and I've got eyes,

536
00:37:44,908 --> 00:37:48,161
and I still see absolutely nothing
but more goddamn sand--

537
00:37:50,998 --> 00:37:51,998
Hold on!

538
00:37:52,666 --> 00:37:53,917
Hold on!

539
00:38:12,769 --> 00:38:14,104
"M" marks the spot.

540
00:38:22,738 --> 00:38:25,824
Vic, do you want
to maybe verbalize something?

541
00:38:25,907 --> 00:38:28,910
It's just unclear what your face
is trying to communicate here.

542
00:38:28,994 --> 00:38:32,956
I know that it's a lot to absorb,
especially all in one go.

543
00:38:33,582 --> 00:38:35,500
Monsters and alternate dimensions,

544
00:38:35,584 --> 00:38:39,171
and I realize that the drugging
of the Turnbows was a bit unethical--

545
00:38:39,254 --> 00:38:44,134
- Okay, stop, Robin. Please, just stop.
- I tried to tell you like a million times.

546
00:38:44,217 --> 00:38:48,013
No, you lied. And then you kept lying
over and over and over again.

547
00:38:48,096 --> 00:38:50,390
- I knew something was wrong.
- I know! I'm sorry!

548
00:38:50,474 --> 00:38:51,993
"Crazy day at work. Call you tomorrow."

549
00:38:52,017 --> 00:38:54,061
"Sorry, there's another crisis
at the Squawk."

550
00:38:54,144 --> 00:38:56,313
I mean, who works all night
at a radio station?

551
00:38:56,396 --> 00:38:59,399
And who is stupid enough to believe that?

552
00:38:59,483 --> 00:39:00,984
Apparently me, Vickie,

553
00:39:01,068 --> 00:39:03,570
who's sitting at home,
waiting for the phone to ring

554
00:39:03,653 --> 00:39:05,573
while you're off with your friends,
getting high.

555
00:39:05,614 --> 00:39:06,740
Getting high?

556
00:39:06,823 --> 00:39:10,369
Come on, Robin.
You are going through withdrawal.

557
00:39:10,452 --> 00:39:12,287
You have the wrong idea.
I am not on drugs.

558
00:39:12,371 --> 00:39:14,081
- Right, sorry.
- Just look at me!

559
00:39:14,164 --> 00:39:17,751
You have been busy with your friends
hunting monsters!

560
00:39:17,834 --> 00:39:20,212
God! All right,
maybe you even believe it yourself.

561
00:39:20,295 --> 00:39:23,757
With the amount that you were clearly on,
if you just go cold turkey,

562
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:26,093
it can cause confusion,
paranoia, hallucinations...

563
00:39:26,176 --> 00:39:29,012
These are not hallucinations!

564
00:39:29,096 --> 00:39:30,806
Okay. So let's recap.

565
00:39:30,889 --> 00:39:33,016
- There is a dark wizard...
- Uh-huh.

566
00:39:33,100 --> 00:39:34,535
- ...who is stealing children...
- Yep.

567
00:39:34,559 --> 00:39:37,020
- ...and putting them in a dream world.
- Right.

568
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:42,150
Vickie, the earth has split in four.

569
00:39:42,234 --> 00:39:44,778
The military has taken over our town.

570
00:39:44,861 --> 00:39:47,322
Is what I'm saying really so insane?

571
00:39:48,532 --> 00:39:49,825
Batshit!

572
00:39:49,908 --> 00:39:52,536
You wanna know
what my face is communicating right now?

573
00:39:52,619 --> 00:39:54,121
- Yes.
- Anger.

574
00:39:54,204 --> 00:39:59,376
But with a dash,
and it is a very, very reluctant dash,

575
00:39:59,459 --> 00:40:00,459
of worry.

576
00:40:01,253 --> 00:40:03,463
Because as furious
as I am with you right now,

577
00:40:03,547 --> 00:40:06,800
you are not well, Robin,
and you need help.

578
00:40:06,883 --> 00:40:08,760
You need serious help.

579
00:40:09,761 --> 00:40:12,097
- I got a call about some drugs...
- Hang on.

580
00:40:12,180 --> 00:40:13,223
Have you seen her?

581
00:40:13,306 --> 00:40:14,307
Robin Buckley?

582
00:40:14,391 --> 00:40:17,269
Yes, she's here. I just saw her go
into that room right there.

583
00:40:19,438 --> 00:40:20,647
Vickie, I'm so sorry.

584
00:40:20,730 --> 00:40:21,565
Don't.

585
00:40:21,648 --> 00:40:23,150
- But I gotta go.
- Robin!

586
00:40:23,859 --> 00:40:24,859
Hey!

587
00:40:25,944 --> 00:40:27,154
Hey, I'm talking to you!

588
00:40:27,821 --> 00:40:28,821
Buckley, stop!

589
00:40:32,659 --> 00:40:34,286
Where do you think you're going?

590
00:40:36,705 --> 00:40:39,040
Help!

591
00:40:39,124 --> 00:40:40,959
- Help!
- Dustin!

592
00:40:41,042 --> 00:40:42,711
- Help! Steve!
- Hey!

593
00:40:46,214 --> 00:40:47,299
Oh, thank you.

594
00:40:49,718 --> 00:40:53,847
Steve, what the hell are you doing?
That's never gonna work. Stop! Stop!

595
00:40:53,930 --> 00:40:57,142
Steve, stop. I'm serious. It's not safe.

596
00:40:57,225 --> 00:40:59,686
- You're gonna fall.
- It's unstable. I got it already, okay?

597
00:40:59,769 --> 00:41:02,355
No, don't! Stop being an asshole!

598
00:41:02,439 --> 00:41:04,149
I'm not. I'm trying to get to them!

599
00:41:04,232 --> 00:41:07,194
You always try to get yourself killed,
and I can't let it happen again.

600
00:41:07,277 --> 00:41:08,862
Stop being so selfish, please.

601
00:41:08,945 --> 00:41:11,823
If you go on there, you're gonna die,
and I can't deal with it again.

602
00:41:11,907 --> 00:41:14,242
You can't die
'cause I can't deal with it again.

603
00:41:14,326 --> 00:41:18,288
Don't let it happen again.
Please. Please don't let it happen again.

604
00:41:19,414 --> 00:41:20,415
Not you.

605
00:41:21,541 --> 00:41:22,626
I'm sorry.

606
00:41:22,709 --> 00:41:23,919
No, no, no.

607
00:41:35,764 --> 00:41:37,390
- Help!
- Help!

608
00:41:37,891 --> 00:41:40,018
- Come on! Help! Hey!
- Help!

609
00:41:40,852 --> 00:41:42,062
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

610
00:41:42,145 --> 00:41:43,647
Down. Get down. Get down.

611
00:41:45,273 --> 00:41:47,984
- What are we doing?
- Sitting spreads our weight out.

612
00:41:48,068 --> 00:41:49,945
Mr. Goldstein, physics.

613
00:41:50,028 --> 00:41:52,364
We can buy ourselves some time.

614
00:41:53,532 --> 00:41:55,492
They must have heard us by now.

615
00:41:55,575 --> 00:41:57,118
Then why haven't they called back?

616
00:41:57,202 --> 00:41:59,454
And even if they did,
what could they even do?

617
00:41:59,538 --> 00:42:01,414
Something. Anything.

618
00:42:01,498 --> 00:42:02,666
Yeah. Yeah.

619
00:42:06,878 --> 00:42:08,046
They're not coming.

620
00:42:08,129 --> 00:42:09,589
Don't say that.

621
00:42:09,673 --> 00:42:11,132
You wanted honesty.

622
00:42:31,319 --> 00:42:32,779
I hate The Clash.

623
00:42:34,948 --> 00:42:35,949
What?

624
00:42:38,410 --> 00:42:40,537
I hate The Clash.

625
00:42:40,620 --> 00:42:44,332
Every time you put them on,
I just try to disassociate from reality.

626
00:42:46,376 --> 00:42:47,460
Yep.

627
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:49,004
I hate reading your articles.

628
00:42:49,087 --> 00:42:50,922
You don't actually wanna hear my thoughts.

629
00:42:51,006 --> 00:42:52,650
You just want me
to tell you they're great.

630
00:42:52,674 --> 00:42:54,050
Because they are.

631
00:42:54,134 --> 00:42:55,176
Most of the time.

632
00:42:55,260 --> 00:42:56,553
Most of the...

633
00:42:56,636 --> 00:42:58,138
Wow. Okay.

634
00:42:59,264 --> 00:43:01,683
I never read <i>Slaughterhouse-Five.</i>

635
00:43:01,766 --> 00:43:04,311
I just read the Cliff notes
and pretended I liked it.

636
00:43:04,394 --> 00:43:05,770
I never read <i>Anna Karenina.</i>

637
00:43:06,479 --> 00:43:08,374
I just read the Cliff notes
and pretended I liked it.

638
00:43:08,398 --> 00:43:10,900
You are always exactly six minutes late,

639
00:43:10,984 --> 00:43:15,030
and I never say anything,
but really, I wanna punch a wall.

640
00:43:15,113 --> 00:43:16,948
I took your pink sweater to Goodwill.

641
00:43:17,032 --> 00:43:18,783
What? I was looking for that.

642
00:43:18,867 --> 00:43:19,993
You know I hate pink.

643
00:43:20,076 --> 00:43:22,495
But I felt guilty afterwards
if that makes you feel better.

644
00:43:22,579 --> 00:43:26,166
I flushed the last bag of
Purple Palm Tree Delight down the toilet,

645
00:43:26,249 --> 00:43:27,917
and I didn't feel guilty about it after.

646
00:43:28,001 --> 00:43:30,170
- Come on.
- I hate it when you're high.

647
00:43:30,253 --> 00:43:31,379
I hate it when you're drunk.

648
00:43:31,463 --> 00:43:34,424
I hate it most of all
when you're high and I'm drunk.

649
00:43:34,507 --> 00:43:35,759
Me too.

650
00:43:36,593 --> 00:43:38,053
Why do we do that?

651
00:43:41,431 --> 00:43:42,515
No idea.

652
00:43:51,232 --> 00:43:52,984
I never applied to Emerson.

653
00:43:55,028 --> 00:43:56,029
I know.

654
00:43:57,906 --> 00:43:59,616
Why didn't you ever say anything?

655
00:44:00,867 --> 00:44:02,285
Why didn't you?

656
00:44:06,081 --> 00:44:07,165
I'm not sure.

657
00:44:13,004 --> 00:44:14,714
I just felt like I was...

658
00:44:16,591 --> 00:44:18,009
doing something wrong.

659
00:44:21,638 --> 00:44:24,808
Like I was going against
the natural order of things.

660
00:44:26,476 --> 00:44:27,686
You know, with...

661
00:44:29,145 --> 00:44:31,606
with what we've been through, it just...

662
00:44:31,690 --> 00:44:33,650
You mean our shared trauma?

663
00:44:35,443 --> 00:44:36,443
Yeah.

664
00:44:38,363 --> 00:44:42,450
How could anyone else possibly understand?

665
00:44:42,534 --> 00:44:43,827
It's like this...

666
00:44:44,911 --> 00:44:46,579
this thing that...

667
00:44:47,997 --> 00:44:50,166
ties us together forever.

668
00:44:51,042 --> 00:44:52,043
You know?

669
00:44:54,170 --> 00:44:56,172
It made me feel safe.

670
00:44:57,298 --> 00:44:58,508
But also...

671
00:45:00,885 --> 00:45:01,885
I don't know.

672
00:45:02,804 --> 00:45:04,180
It can be suffocating.

673
00:45:05,932 --> 00:45:06,933
Yeah.

674
00:45:10,937 --> 00:45:12,147
That spring break,

675
00:45:13,314 --> 00:45:15,108
when you were in Lenora...

676
00:45:16,693 --> 00:45:19,320
I didn't really have to stay behind
to work.

677
00:45:19,404 --> 00:45:21,990
I could have had Fred cover for me.

678
00:45:24,451 --> 00:45:26,703
But I think that's why I stayed.

679
00:45:28,204 --> 00:45:29,914
That feeling that I just...

680
00:45:30,749 --> 00:45:31,958
I needed space.

681
00:45:34,586 --> 00:45:36,463
Space to be with someone else?

682
00:45:42,010 --> 00:45:43,553
Steve's a good guy.

683
00:45:45,472 --> 00:45:46,765
He makes me laugh.

684
00:45:47,891 --> 00:45:52,479
And, he has better hair than you.
Like, way better.

685
00:45:53,354 --> 00:45:54,397
But no.

686
00:45:56,900 --> 00:45:59,194
No, it was never like that with him.

687
00:45:59,778 --> 00:46:01,654
We're just different people.

688
00:46:01,738 --> 00:46:05,450
You know what he told me?
He wants six kids.

689
00:46:05,533 --> 00:46:06,659
Six kids?

690
00:46:06,743 --> 00:46:08,912
Six little nuggets.

691
00:46:09,788 --> 00:46:11,122
That's like a Happy Meal.

692
00:46:12,707 --> 00:46:14,042
But my point is...

693
00:46:15,502 --> 00:46:18,963
he knows what he wants, and that's great.

694
00:46:19,047 --> 00:46:20,381
But I...

695
00:46:21,216 --> 00:46:22,217
don't.

696
00:46:24,010 --> 00:46:25,303
And...

697
00:46:25,970 --> 00:46:28,932
I guess I was hoping
I'd have time to figure that out.

698
00:46:30,183 --> 00:46:32,727
- But then...
- The world split in four.

699
00:46:32,811 --> 00:46:34,145
And now...

700
00:46:36,856 --> 00:46:37,982
And now...

701
00:46:42,570 --> 00:46:43,570
Hey...

702
00:46:48,785 --> 00:46:50,703
One last confession.

703
00:46:51,788 --> 00:46:53,122
A big one.

704
00:46:59,712 --> 00:47:01,256
John Coltrane.

705
00:47:01,881 --> 00:47:03,383
I figure that...

706
00:47:04,509 --> 00:47:06,177
I've screwed up enough with you.

707
00:47:08,471 --> 00:47:11,349
It'd be nice to get something right
for once in the end.

708
00:47:12,392 --> 00:47:13,393
Here.

709
00:47:31,369 --> 00:47:32,787
Nancy Wheeler.

710
00:47:35,331 --> 00:47:36,416
Will you...

711
00:47:38,293 --> 00:47:39,294
not...

712
00:47:40,128 --> 00:47:41,129
marry me?

713
00:47:48,136 --> 00:47:50,305
I tried to convince myself

714
00:47:51,472 --> 00:47:53,308
that this would somehow

715
00:47:54,100 --> 00:47:55,643
fix everything.

716
00:47:55,727 --> 00:47:58,354
But it was just gonna make things worse.

717
00:47:59,480 --> 00:48:02,942
Which is why it has been sitting
like a cannonball in my pocket

718
00:48:03,026 --> 00:48:04,527
for the last two days.

719
00:48:07,322 --> 00:48:08,573
So what do you say?

720
00:48:12,744 --> 00:48:14,787
Do you accept my un-proposal?

721
00:48:15,997 --> 00:48:17,957
I accept your un-proposal.

722
00:48:20,376 --> 00:48:21,502
I loved you.

723
00:48:22,837 --> 00:48:24,005
I love you,

724
00:48:24,839 --> 00:48:25,965
Nancy Wheeler.

725
00:48:27,467 --> 00:48:29,844
I love you, Jonathan Byers.

726
00:49:05,630 --> 00:49:06,798
Oh my God.

727
00:49:15,932 --> 00:49:16,975
Jonathan!

728
00:49:17,558 --> 00:49:18,559
Oh my God!

729
00:49:21,646 --> 00:49:22,647
My God.

730
00:49:49,674 --> 00:49:50,925
Thank you.

731
00:49:51,009 --> 00:49:52,593
I will find him.

732
00:49:54,095 --> 00:49:55,722
I will bring him home.

733
00:50:03,396 --> 00:50:06,232
Okay. Now remember,
if you want out of there...

734
00:50:35,595 --> 00:50:37,430
Will, I'm here.

735
00:50:39,348 --> 00:50:41,768
I need you to show me where you are.

736
00:50:43,394 --> 00:50:45,229
Show me where you are.

737
00:51:06,334 --> 00:51:07,335
Will.

738
00:51:10,630 --> 00:51:11,631
Will.

739
00:51:12,215 --> 00:51:13,424
Will, can you hear me?

740
00:51:13,508 --> 00:51:14,759
Will, wake up!

741
00:51:42,954 --> 00:51:44,080
Can I have that?

742
00:51:52,004 --> 00:51:53,589
Do you think someone fell?

743
00:51:58,052 --> 00:52:00,721
It... It's just a memory, right?

744
00:52:00,805 --> 00:52:02,682
Nothing in here can hurt us.

745
00:52:02,765 --> 00:52:04,100
Nothing can hurt us.

746
00:52:18,030 --> 00:52:19,323
Just stay behind me, okay?

747
00:52:19,407 --> 00:52:21,325
- But you said--
- I know what I said.

748
00:52:33,421 --> 00:52:34,797
How did you find me?

749
00:52:37,133 --> 00:52:39,135
How did you find me?

750
00:52:39,218 --> 00:52:42,138
He sees us. He sees us.
How does he see us?

751
00:52:42,221 --> 00:52:43,389
I won't hurt you.

752
00:52:44,056 --> 00:52:46,851
Please, mister, don't shoot.

753
00:52:46,934 --> 00:52:48,186
Who are you?

754
00:52:48,269 --> 00:52:50,855
Henry. Henry Creel. I live near here.

755
00:52:50,938 --> 00:52:52,982
- Who sent you?
- Nobody sent me.

756
00:52:53,065 --> 00:52:55,265
- They sent you.
- I was in the caves. I heard a scream.

757
00:52:55,318 --> 00:52:56,527
They sent you!

758
00:52:56,611 --> 00:52:59,697
You're just confused. You need a doctor.

759
00:53:13,794 --> 00:53:15,671
Please! Please!

760
00:53:24,180 --> 00:53:25,180
Holly!

761
00:53:26,098 --> 00:53:27,099
Holly!

762
00:53:31,437 --> 00:53:32,438
Shit!

763
00:53:34,357 --> 00:53:36,901
Hey, it's okay. It's okay.

764
00:53:36,984 --> 00:53:41,364
Why did that man try to hurt Henry?
Hurt Henry? He was only trying to help.

765
00:53:41,447 --> 00:53:43,366
- I don't know.
- Is this what made Henry bad?

766
00:53:43,449 --> 00:53:47,161
I don't know. But it's over now, okay?
We have to keep moving.

767
00:54:37,503 --> 00:54:38,713
You were right.

768
00:54:38,796 --> 00:54:41,549
The way out of Camazotz, it's here.

769
00:54:43,009 --> 00:54:47,138
<i>♪ Be runnin' up that road
Be runnin' up that hill ♪</i>

770
00:54:50,474 --> 00:54:51,474
Max?

771
00:54:53,728 --> 00:54:59,400
<i>♪ ...make a deal with God
And I'd get Him to swap our places ♪</i>

772
00:55:01,861 --> 00:55:08,576
<i>You are going
to spy for me one last time.</i>

773
00:55:20,087 --> 00:55:21,088
Found you.

774
00:55:22,882 --> 00:55:26,510
Will. Will, it's okay.
It's okay. I'm here.

775
00:55:26,594 --> 00:55:27,595
- El...
- I'm here.

776
00:55:27,678 --> 00:55:28,846
El... El...

777
00:55:28,929 --> 00:55:32,433
It's me. It's me.
I'm here to bring you home. It's okay.

778
00:55:32,516 --> 00:55:35,644
I tried to stop him, but I couldn't.

779
00:55:35,728 --> 00:55:36,729
He saw.

780
00:55:37,313 --> 00:55:39,023
He saw what? What did he see?

781
00:55:39,732 --> 00:55:40,732
Max.

782
00:55:41,859 --> 00:55:43,402
He knows where she is now.

783
00:55:44,111 --> 00:55:45,863
And he sent them after her.

784
00:55:46,739 --> 00:55:49,408
They're coming for her. In Hawkins.

785
00:55:53,371 --> 00:55:54,497
- El!
- El, what's up?

786
00:55:54,580 --> 00:55:55,580
Are you okay?

787
00:55:56,248 --> 00:55:57,249
El, what's wrong?

788
00:55:57,333 --> 00:55:59,335
- Is he all right?
- Yeah.

789
00:55:59,418 --> 00:56:01,921
Vecna's going to kill Max.

790
00:56:02,505 --> 00:56:04,590
We have to get to the hospital right now.

791
00:56:04,673 --> 00:56:07,385
Hey! Are you deaf or what?
She's in withdrawal.

792
00:56:07,468 --> 00:56:08,945
- I am not.
- You know what that means?

793
00:56:08,969 --> 00:56:11,055
She needs to be in a hospital,
not a prison.

794
00:56:11,138 --> 00:56:13,182
Would you look at that?
She's in a hospital.

795
00:56:13,265 --> 00:56:16,185
This is Hawkins, Candy Cane.
Not our first junkie.

796
00:56:21,440 --> 00:56:23,359
Power outage in a hospital.

797
00:56:23,943 --> 00:56:26,237
Can't be good for Granny. Not our problem.

798
00:56:26,320 --> 00:56:27,964
You don't understand. We need to evacuate.

799
00:56:27,988 --> 00:56:30,699
We don't need to do shit.
Keep moving, junkie.

800
00:56:30,783 --> 00:56:32,159
I'm not a junkie.

801
00:56:32,243 --> 00:56:34,453
If we don't get everyone
out of here right now,

802
00:56:34,537 --> 00:56:36,497
we are all going to die.

803
00:56:36,580 --> 00:56:39,291
There is nothing you can say
on God's green earth

804
00:56:39,375 --> 00:56:43,003
that is going to keep you out of a cell.
So save your junkie breath.

805
00:56:43,087 --> 00:56:45,881
- We need to evacuate.
- I actually don't need to do shit.

806
00:56:48,467 --> 00:56:49,343
Holy shit!

807
00:56:49,427 --> 00:56:50,428
Run!

808
00:57:13,534 --> 00:57:15,077
They're not after us.

809
00:57:15,161 --> 00:57:16,161
Huh? What?

810
00:57:16,203 --> 00:57:19,206
They're not after us.
Do you know another way out?

811
00:57:19,290 --> 00:57:21,584
The basement. The basement!
It leads to staff parking.

812
00:57:23,711 --> 00:57:24,712
Okay.

813
00:57:25,254 --> 00:57:27,298
Come on, Lucas, pick up. Pick up.

814
00:57:30,301 --> 00:57:32,052
Pick up. Pick up. What are you doing?

815
00:57:32,136 --> 00:57:33,405
- Can those things understand English?
- No.

816
00:57:33,429 --> 00:57:35,269
- Then this doesn't need to be private.
- What?

817
00:57:36,432 --> 00:57:38,642
<i>Lucas, it's Robin.
A Demo is headed your way.</i>

818
00:57:38,726 --> 00:57:41,886
Do you hear me? A Demo is headed your way.
You need to get Max out of there now.

819
00:57:41,937 --> 00:57:43,856
<i>Take the elevator.
They're on the stairwell.</i>

820
00:57:43,939 --> 00:57:45,274
We'll meet you in the basement.

821
00:58:12,134 --> 00:58:13,177
Come on. Come on.

822
00:58:23,229 --> 00:58:24,313
Shit.

823
00:58:25,564 --> 00:58:26,564
Shit. Come on!

824
00:58:44,542 --> 00:58:46,043
Goddamnit!

825
00:58:47,753 --> 00:58:48,963
It's not budging.

826
00:58:49,046 --> 00:58:51,298
We're just gonna have to try, okay?

827
00:58:51,382 --> 00:58:52,383
Come on.

828
00:58:58,097 --> 00:58:59,098
You good?

829
00:58:59,181 --> 00:59:00,558
- I... I'm good.
- Okay.

830
00:59:04,270 --> 00:59:06,939
- I need you to grab my hand, okay?
- Okay.

831
00:59:30,421 --> 00:59:31,297
Whoa! Jesus!

832
00:59:31,380 --> 00:59:32,840
Okay. They're coming!

833
00:59:32,923 --> 00:59:34,300
- We gotta go!
- Which way?

834
00:59:35,759 --> 00:59:38,137
Here! What the hell is going on?

835
00:59:39,430 --> 00:59:41,056
- Here!
- How are they finding us?

836
00:59:41,140 --> 00:59:42,850
I don't know,
but we gotta get out of here.

837
00:59:42,933 --> 00:59:43,809
Okay. Come on.

838
00:59:43,892 --> 00:59:45,728
- Come on. Let's go.
- Go, go, go.

839
00:59:45,811 --> 00:59:48,230
Come on. Shut the door. Shut the door!

840
00:59:50,691 --> 00:59:52,735
- Oh, shit.
- Go! Just keep going!

841
00:59:53,694 --> 00:59:54,987
- Come on.
- Damn it!

842
00:59:55,070 --> 00:59:56,655
We gotta go!

843
00:59:57,740 --> 01:00:00,242
- The door! Open the door!
- Go, go, go!

844
01:00:05,414 --> 01:00:07,750
Shit. This way, guys! Come on! Come on!

845
01:00:07,833 --> 01:00:08,833
Get down!

846
01:00:15,549 --> 01:00:18,010
<i>♪ If I only could... ♪</i>

847
01:00:18,093 --> 01:00:20,804
I'm really sorry
I thought you were a druggie.

848
01:00:22,056 --> 01:00:26,644
I'm sorry for lying to you for, like,
a ludicrously extended period of time.

849
01:00:27,144 --> 01:00:30,731
For the record,
I wasn't lying about Enzo's.

850
01:00:30,814 --> 01:00:35,569
And if by some miracle we survive this,
I am going to take you there,

851
01:00:35,653 --> 01:00:39,573
and we are getting dessert. Deal?

852
01:00:39,657 --> 01:00:42,743
<i>♪ Unaware I'm tearin' you asunder
Yeah, yeah, yo ♪</i>

853
01:00:43,577 --> 01:00:45,871
<i>♪ There is thunder in our hearts ♪</i>

854
01:01:03,180 --> 01:01:05,224
<i>♪ It's you and me ♪</i>

855
01:01:05,307 --> 01:01:06,725
We have to turn it off.

856
01:01:06,809 --> 01:01:10,312
We can't. We can't.
No. No. Max is coming back.

857
01:01:10,896 --> 01:01:12,064
We have to.

858
01:01:13,065 --> 01:01:14,358
She's coming back.

859
01:01:14,441 --> 01:01:16,443
<i>♪ Come on, darlin' ♪</i>

860
01:01:21,365 --> 01:01:22,491
Are you okay?

861
01:01:23,951 --> 01:01:24,993
Go.

862
01:01:35,713 --> 01:01:36,755
Okay.

863
01:01:40,551 --> 01:01:42,428
You ready to go home, tourist?

864
01:01:45,097 --> 01:01:46,097
Yeah.

865
01:01:46,682 --> 01:01:50,352
<i>♪ If I only could make a deal with God ♪</i>

866
01:01:50,436 --> 01:01:53,564
<i>♪ I'd get him to swap our places ♪</i>

867
01:01:54,773 --> 01:01:58,527
<i>♪ Be runnin' up that road
Be runnin' up that hill ♪</i>

868
01:02:03,824 --> 01:02:07,995
<i>♪ If I only could make a deal with God ♪</i>

869
01:02:08,078 --> 01:02:11,331
<i>♪ I'd get him to swap our places ♪</i>

870
01:02:11,415 --> 01:02:15,794
<i>♪ Be runnin' up that road
Be runnin' up that hill ♪</i>

871
01:02:15,878 --> 01:02:17,880
<i>♪ Be runnin' up that building ♪</i>

872
01:04:11,702 --> 01:04:15,581
<i>♪ Let's exchange the experience ♪</i>

873
01:04:25,716 --> 01:04:26,758
Lucas.

874
01:04:33,473 --> 01:04:35,017
Holly. Wait.

875
01:04:37,352 --> 01:04:38,395
You can't come with me.

876
01:04:38,478 --> 01:04:41,273
What? What do you mean?

877
01:04:41,356 --> 01:04:42,733
This way leads to me,

878
01:04:43,609 --> 01:04:46,361
to my body, not yours.

879
01:04:46,445 --> 01:04:48,071
You have to find your own way.

880
01:04:48,155 --> 01:04:51,700
How? I don't have Kate Bush.
I don't even know who Kate Bush is.

881
01:04:51,783 --> 01:04:53,702
You don't need Kate Bush
to get out of here.

882
01:04:53,785 --> 01:04:55,787
Turns out, I don't either.

883
01:04:55,871 --> 01:04:58,165
Music isn't the only way back.

884
01:04:58,707 --> 01:05:03,170
You just need something that connects you
to the real world, to home.

885
01:05:03,837 --> 01:05:05,672
Something powerful,

886
01:05:06,256 --> 01:05:07,507
meaningful.

887
01:05:07,591 --> 01:05:11,219
Lucas, when... when he took my hand
in the hospital,

888
01:05:12,179 --> 01:05:14,806
I could feel it. Right here.

889
01:05:16,141 --> 01:05:18,602
But then I could also feel it in here.

890
01:05:19,311 --> 01:05:20,896
But I don't have a boyfriend.

891
01:05:20,979 --> 01:05:22,314
You don't need a boyfriend.

892
01:05:22,397 --> 01:05:24,441
You just need something
that's special to you,

893
01:05:24,524 --> 01:05:27,569
something that makes you feel safe,

894
01:05:27,653 --> 01:05:31,698
something that brings you strength,
something that gives you hope.

895
01:05:32,282 --> 01:05:33,492
Holly the Heroic.

896
01:05:33,575 --> 01:05:35,327
She's here with you now.

897
01:05:36,620 --> 01:05:38,789
But she's also with you in the real world.

898
01:05:38,872 --> 01:05:42,793
Wherever you are,
all you have to do is follow her home.

899
01:05:42,876 --> 01:05:43,961
How?

900
01:05:44,711 --> 01:05:49,633
Just... try and remember
what it is that she means to you.

901
01:05:50,676 --> 01:05:52,886
She doesn't mean anything important.

902
01:05:55,097 --> 01:05:56,390
She's just a toy.

903
01:05:57,474 --> 01:06:00,352
If she's just a toy,
why do you always carry her with you?

904
01:06:00,435 --> 01:06:01,895
Mike.

905
01:06:01,979 --> 01:06:05,607
He said that she had divine powers
and that she never gets scared,

906
01:06:05,691 --> 01:06:09,653
and so if I ever got scared,
I could just... become her.

907
01:06:09,736 --> 01:06:13,240
But I keep trying, and it never works.

908
01:06:15,367 --> 01:06:17,369
No matter what I do, I'm still me.

909
01:06:19,621 --> 01:06:22,207
The girl who needs a stupid night-light.

910
01:06:22,290 --> 01:06:25,335
When my mom was attacked,
I couldn't save her.

911
01:06:25,419 --> 01:06:26,712
I couldn't even save myself.

912
01:06:26,795 --> 01:06:28,380
Holly, get back!

913
01:06:29,631 --> 01:06:31,550
I just stood there.

914
01:06:31,633 --> 01:06:33,552
And then when Henry attacked you...

915
01:06:34,219 --> 01:06:35,846
Stop!

916
01:06:35,929 --> 01:06:40,767
I stood there again.
There's nothing heroic about that.

917
01:06:41,351 --> 01:06:44,229
There was nothing that you could do
in those moments, Holly.

918
01:06:44,312 --> 01:06:47,399
I mean, you're a Wheeler. You're smart.

919
01:06:48,150 --> 01:06:51,737
You honestly think that you could've
stopped those monsters with a fire poker?

920
01:06:52,320 --> 01:06:55,115
And I think you're leaving
a few important things out.

921
01:06:55,198 --> 01:06:57,909
The day that we met,
you went into the woods

922
01:06:57,993 --> 01:07:00,579
even though Henry told you
that dangerous monsters live there.

923
01:07:00,662 --> 01:07:03,040
And then you followed me into the cave

924
01:07:03,123 --> 01:07:05,709
even though you had no good reason
to trust me.

925
01:07:05,792 --> 01:07:08,962
And then when I told you
to go back to Henry,

926
01:07:09,046 --> 01:07:10,505
to go back into danger,

927
01:07:10,589 --> 01:07:11,882
you didn't hesitate.

928
01:07:11,965 --> 01:07:15,844
And today, when I gave up, you didn't.

929
01:07:17,429 --> 01:07:19,556
I've been here for so long, Holly.

930
01:07:20,932 --> 01:07:22,017
So long.

931
01:07:24,061 --> 01:07:25,896
And I could never make it out.

932
01:07:27,814 --> 01:07:29,274
But you?

933
01:07:30,067 --> 01:07:32,402
You found a way through Camazotz.

934
01:07:32,486 --> 01:07:33,737
Because of you...

935
01:07:35,113 --> 01:07:36,656
I get to see my friends.

936
01:07:37,908 --> 01:07:39,242
I get to see Lucas.

937
01:07:41,203 --> 01:07:43,497
You saved me, Holly Wheeler.

938
01:07:44,998 --> 01:07:46,083
You saved me.

939
01:07:48,335 --> 01:07:52,631
So you see,
Holly the Heroic is not just a toy.

940
01:07:54,549 --> 01:07:56,051
She's you, Holly.

941
01:07:57,719 --> 01:07:58,720
She's you.

942
01:08:18,782 --> 01:08:20,534
How did you know that would work?

943
01:08:22,285 --> 01:08:23,745
I didn't.

944
01:08:26,081 --> 01:08:30,544
You still have a long journey ahead.
I don't know where you're gonna wake up.

945
01:08:30,627 --> 01:08:32,712
But I figure Vecna's holding you
in the Upside Down.

946
01:08:32,796 --> 01:08:36,967
But remember, the Upside Down,
it's just like Hawkins.

947
01:08:37,050 --> 01:08:39,970
So find your way back to your house
and hide there.

948
01:08:40,053 --> 01:08:42,305
We will come and find you. Okay?

949
01:08:58,780 --> 01:09:00,240
I'll see you on the other side.

950
01:09:00,907 --> 01:09:02,033
On the other side.

951
01:09:27,309 --> 01:09:31,313
<i>♪ If I only could make a deal with God ♪</i>

952
01:09:31,396 --> 01:09:35,192
<i>♪ I'd get him to swap our places ♪</i>

953
01:09:35,775 --> 01:09:40,030
<i>♪ Be runnin' up that road
Be runnin' up that hill ♪</i>

954
01:09:40,864 --> 01:09:43,825
<i>♪ With no problems ♪</i>

955
01:09:43,909 --> 01:09:48,163
<i>♪ Be runnin' up that road
Be runnin' up that hill ♪</i>

956
01:09:48,705 --> 01:09:52,250
<i>♪ With no problems ♪</i>

